# Each person has a mother named by a Skolem IRI. The role and person form
# the key, so Ann and Bob get different mother IRIs, and a second rule adds
# reciprocal child links. The computed name is bound in the premise, making
# this an ordinary forward rule with a strictly checkable proof.

@prefix : <http://example.org/people#>.
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#>.

:ann a :Person.
:bob a :Person.

{ ?p a :Person. (:mother ?p) log:skolem ?m } => { ?p :mother ?m. ?m a :Woman }.
{ ?p :mother ?m } => { ?m :hasChild ?p }.
